# Accepted risks for the container scan — TEMPORARY, reviewed on every change.
# Remove an entry as soon as a fixed upstream release ships.
#
# All findings are pip's OWN vendored copies, not application dependencies.
# pip 26.2 (2026-07-29) began shipping a CycloneDX SBOM of its vendored
# libraries (pip/_vendor/bom.cdx.json); trivy ingests in-image SBOMs, so these
# internal copies became visible to the scan even though nothing in this
# project installs or imports them. A bare `python:3.12-slim` image with only
# `pip install --upgrade pip` reproduced exactly the msgpack and setuptools
# findings when they first appeared (2026-08-03).

# setuptools: pip vendors only the pkg_resources subpackage — the vulnerable
# PackageIndex/easy_install code path is not shipped in the image.
# pip 26.3, the newest pip on 2026-11-02, still pins setuptools==70.3.0 in
# pip/_vendor/vendor.txt. Its msgpack 1.2.4 and urllib3 2.8.0 are fixed, so
# those entries were removed that day.
CVE-2025-47273
